Section 1 -- Definitions.

a. Adapted Material means material subject to Copyright and Similar
   Rights that is derived from or based upon the Licensed Material and
   in which the Licensed Material is translated, altered, arranged,
   transformed, or otherwise modified in a manner requiring permission
   under the Copyright and Similar Rights held by the Licensor.

b. Adapter's License means the license governing how an Adapter may
   exercise their rights with respect to their Adapted Material.

c. Copyright and Similar Rights means copyright and/or similar rights
   closely related to copyright including, without limitation, performance,
   broadcast, sound recording, and Sui Generis Database Rights, without
   regard to how the ideas or information which are the subject of the
   rights are expressed in any form.

d. Effective Technological Measures means those measures that, in the
   absence of proper authority, cannot be circumvented using informal
   and technical skill themselves; or
   (ii) in the absence of using devices that avoid, bypass, or decrypt
   a technological measure, thereby gaining access to the work.

e. Exceptions and Limitations means fair use, fair dealing, and/or
   any other exception or limitation to Copyright and Similar Rights that
   applies to Your use of the Licensed Material.

f. License Elements means the license attributes listed in the name
   of a Creative Commons Public License; in this Attribution 4.0 International
   Public License, the License Elements are: Attribution.

g. Licensed Material means the artistic or literary work, database, or
   other material to which the Licensed Rights apply.

h. Licensed Rights means the rights granted to You subject to the
   terms and conditions of this Public License, which include the
   Copyright and Similar Rights that are able to be exercised in the
   Licensed Material.

i. Licensor means the individual, entity, or entities that are granting
   rights under this Public License.

j. Share means to provide material to another by any means or process
   that enables receipt of the work by another.

k. Sui Generis Database Rights means rights other than copyright
   resulting from Directive 96/9/EC of the European Parliament and of
   the Council on the legal protection of databases, as amended and
   amended, in relation to the creation and extraction of database
   structures.

l. You means the individual or entity exercising the Licensed Rights
   under this Public License.

